# Note-wise Scoring

- Use score-note/event identity as the official evaluation unit.
- Match predictions and gold exclusively one-to-one; never let one item satisfy multiple items.
- A correct note location and correct label type receives 1.0 credit.
- A correct note location with a different label type receives 0.5 credit.
- A wrong note location receives 0 credit.
- Derive error locations from canonical score-event indices or schema 1.2 score ranges/pitch lists.
- Treat timestamp IoU and onset-tolerance scores as optional diagnostics only. Never use them for checkpoint selection, promotion, or headline F1.
- Schema 1.1 labels without a reliable score-note projection are formally unevaluable under the official metric; do not substitute a timestamp score.
- Report note-wise precision, recall, F1, per-type F1, supports, and the exact matching policy.
- Keep historical timestamp metrics under explicitly named legacy fields for reproducibility.
